                <pb facs="0464" n="382" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg382"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.6176 F 51/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The General Receiver of Customs of Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">De la Rue</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of the Division of Western European
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Castle</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1924-10-29T21:05:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1924-10-01T00:00:00-00:44"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>].<lb/>[Received October 29, 1924—9:05
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Considering local political and international situation is there any way
                    obtaining from Firestone indication of their decision in time for December
                    legislature? Government without information. Further delay might involve failure
                    decisive action until December 1925. Fear question if asked might be
                    misinterpreted as an official attempt force their decision.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. De la Rue</hi></signed>]<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">General Receiver</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
